<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | GPABound" description="Learn how GPABound handles calculator entries, requests, analytics, and advertising data.">
  <article class="wrap legal-page"><span class="eyebrow">LEGAL</span><h1>Privacy policy</h1><p class="lead">A plain-language explanation of what this site collects and why.</p><p class="updated">Last updated: September 25, 2026</p>
    <h2>Calculator data</h2><p>Course names, grades, credits, and previous GPA values entered into the calculator are processed in your browser. The current prototype does not transmit or store those entries on our servers.</p>
    <h2>Scale requests</h2><p>In the current prototype, requests submitted through the “Request a scale” dialog are saved in your browser’s local storage. They are not sent to us until a form-processing service is connected. You can remove them by clearing this site’s browser data.</p>
    <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2><p>We do not currently load analytics or advertising scripts. If these services are introduced, this policy and any required consent controls will be updated before deployment.</p>
    <h2>Cookies</h2><p>The current site does not set advertising cookies. Hosting providers may keep short-lived technical logs for security and service reliability.</p>
    <h2>External links</h2><p>Links to universities and other websites are governed by those sites’ own privacy policies.</p>
    <h2>Your choices</h2><p>You can use the calculator without creating an account. You may disable local storage in your browser, though request-saving features may no longer work.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2><p>Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href="mailto:hello@gpabound.com">hello@gpabound.com</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
